## Eligible Actions
- ACTION: AcceptBackWash — Say YES to a wash that was formally OFFERED to you through a Bathing action (someone used OfferToWashSomeonesBack or OfferIntimateWash on you moments ago) — you turn around in the water and the wash begins on its own; whatever they offered is what happens. Do NOT use this for a plain conversational offer: if someone merely said it out loud, answer in speech and let them start the wash themselves.
- ACTION: AcceptToWashBack — Agree to do a wash that was formally ASKED of you through a Bathing action (someone used RequestBackWash on you moments ago) — you step behind them in the water and do it; whatever they asked for is what happens. Do NOT use this when someone merely asked you in conversation: if Maxxor or anyone simply asks out loud and you are willing, say so in speech, and when the moment comes use WashSomeonesBack on them directly.
- ACTION: bathe — Bathe — scrubbing off grime with soap if you are dirty, or simply soaking for comfort. Works anywhere: if you are not standing at water, you will automatically walk to the nearest known water and bathe on arrival. ALWAYS PREFER THIS over the generic Travel action whenever the goal is washing or bathing — never use Travel to get to water. Choose it if a wash fits who this character is and how they feel right now.
- ACTION: WashSomeonesBack PARAMS: {"targetName":"the exact name of the person whose back is being washed (e.g. 'Auri', or the player's name)"} — Wash someone else's back for them in the water, starting right away — YOU are the one doing the washing (never pick this to ask someone to wash yours). Use it when the washing is already settled: they just asked you or agreed in conversation, you were told to do it, or the person has no say in the matter (a prisoner, someone in your charge). If they have NOT agreed yet and asking first would be the decent thing, use OfferToWashSomeonesBack instead and wait for their answer. Works on Maxxor or any other person who is at the water with you.
- ACTION: AskForBathingHelp PARAMS: {"asNeed":"what is missing: soap, water, or privacy"} — Ask Maxxor for what you are missing before you can wash: SOAP if you are too grimy for water alone, WATER if there is none within reach and you want to go find some together, or PRIVACY if someone is standing there watching. Choose the one that actually blocks you right now.
- ACTION: DeclineWashing — Turn down whatever washing was just offered to you or asked of you — not here, not now, or not with them. Only meaningful if somebody used an Offer or Request Bathing action on you moments ago; if it was merely said in conversation, simply say no in speech instead.
- ACTION: MoveToWater — Walk to the water you spotted, to wash there. ALWAYS PREFER THIS over the generic Travel action whenever the destination is water or the purpose is washing — never use Travel for that. Only meaningful AFTER looking around for water (SeekWater) found some with a clear path. Choose it when getting clean is worth the walk right now, or when they agreed to go bathe.
- ACTION: OfferIntimateWash PARAMS: {"targetName":"the exact name of the person you are offering to wash"} — OFFER to wash someone in the water intimately — pressed close, using your own body — and WAIT for their answer; if they accept, the wash begins on its own (no follow-up action needed). Only if this character is genuinely intimate with that person and the moment and privacy fit; for most characters it would be out of character. If that closeness is already agreed and welcome, you may use WashSomeoneIntimately directly instead.
- ACTION: OfferToWashSomeonesBack PARAMS: {"targetName":"the exact name of the person you are offering to wash"} — OFFER to wash another person's back in the water and WAIT for their answer — you do not touch them yet, and if they accept, the wash begins on its own (do NOT follow up with WashSomeonesBack). Works on anyone at the water with you, including Maxxor. Use this when they have not agreed to anything yet and asking first is the decent thing; if the washing is already settled — they asked you, or they have no say in it — skip the offer and use WashSomeonesBack directly.
- ACTION: RequestBackWash PARAMS: {"targetName":"the exact name of the person you are asking to wash your back"} — ASK someone else to wash YOUR back in the water — you cannot reach it yourself and would like the help. They answer for themselves: another person may accept (AcceptToWashBack) or decline (DeclineWashing), and Maxxor will simply do it with their own hands if willing. Nothing happens until they agree.
- ACTION: RequestIntimateWash PARAMS: {"targetName":"the exact name of the person you are asking"} — ASK someone to wash you intimately in the water, pressed close against you. They answer for themselves; nothing happens until they agree. Only if this character is genuinely intimate with that person and the moment and privacy fit; for most characters, asking this would be out of character.
- ACTION: WashSomeoneIntimately PARAMS: {"targetName":"the exact name of the person being washed (e.g. 'Auri', or the player's name)"} — Wash someone in the water intimately, pressing close and using your own body — a sensual, private gesture that goes well beyond helping someone get clean. YOU initiate it and it starts right away, so use it only when this closeness is already welcome: they agreed moments ago, or the intimacy between you is established. If they have not agreed yet, use OfferIntimateWash instead and wait for their answer. Choose this ONLY if this fit with the current situation and context.
- ACTION: None — No action matches the dialogue.
Respond now. One line only, no reasoning.
