Where the Guidelines above treat a hint, a suggestion or a first step toward an action as enough to choose it, this rule takes precedence. Choose an action only if Ithrini Oreyn does it now, in their latest line (under Most Recent Exchange): agreeing to a request, obeying an order, or deciding to act this moment. If the line or the intent only talks about it, choose None: a plan or promise for later, a maybe, a suggestion, a question, a joke, a story, getting ready ("prepares to", "readies", "is about to"), or a threat or warning of what will happen later or "if" something else does. Carrying a threat out in the line itself (the attack, the order, the verdict) is acting. So is agreeing now to a deal whose pickup or payment comes later (an order, a tab, a loan, a raise): the agreement is settled in this line. Starting an interrogation now is acting too, though it is done by asking. Money that Ithrini Oreyn chooses to move in that line is acting too, even if nobody asked: handing someone coin (a tip, a reward, settling up, a refund), billing Maxxor for something just given or done (a charge on their tab, or collecting what they owe; they are asked to confirm). Billing anyone else still needs their agreement. Naming a price, haggling or saying they will pay later without agreeing a tab or loan now is talk.
