- ACTION: Journeys — Category: the speaker sets off on foot for another place right now, ahead of the player or without them (sent on ahead to wait there, or leaving on their own business), or changes pace on, or calls off, a trip already under way, a camp trip included. Only for a departure in this line: plans, maybes, 'we could go', questions and a place merely coming up are talk. Going together is not a departure: someone already walking with the player just comes along, and agreeing now to come along is TagAlong or Companionship. Setting off for the player's camp or base is Camping; a guard going to arrest or search someone is Arrest.
- ACTION: Companionship — Category: the player's companions and anyone walking along with the player: someone joins the player as a companion; someone walking with the player waits at this spot, or follows again after waiting; a companion parts ways and goes home, or quits for good after long mistreatment; the place where the player and a companion are standing becomes that companion's home. Only for a decision made in this line; talk of someday is not. Walking along for a short while without joining is TagAlong.
- ACTION: Bathing — Washing and water — bathe yourself, scrub someone else's back, look for water or walk to it, or ask for the soap, water or privacy you need to get clean. SELECT THIS for anything to do with getting clean or going to water; never use the generic Travel action to reach water.
- ACTION: Brawl — Category: a fist-fight, fists only, that ends when someone drops or gives up, never in death: dare someone present to one, answer a dare (accept or refuse), or give up a fist-fight already under way. Only for the dare, the answer or the surrender in this line; teasing, boasts and 'I could take you' are words. Armed fights are Combat.
- ACTION: Captives — Category: seizing people and handling the captives the speaker's side holds, not a lawful arrest: bind someone here and lead them away; abduct a named person to a place; or, for a captive already held, free them, loosen their bonds, move them, tie them to furniture, question them, or send a ransom demand. Only when it happens now, on an order or the speaker's own decision in this line; threats, jokes and plans for later are talk. Arresting someone for the jail is Arrest.
- ACTION: leashed_leashSubject PARAMS: {"intent":"Who you collar, who holds it (you / another / None / tied), how, and why. Example — put a rope leash on Tom's neck and hold it myself."} — You put a new collar and leash on someone nearby. Hold it, leave it hanging, or tie them to a point. Not when you are the one getting collared, and not for changing or removing an existing leash.
- ACTION: Combat — Category: a real fight with weapons or magic: attack someone this very moment, or end a fight the speaker is in by surrendering or calling a truce. Carrying on a fight already under way needs no action. Threats of what will happen, warnings, readying a weapon, 'prepare to fight' and 'if you…' are words; drawing steel and striking now is the attack. Fist-fights are Brawl; an outlaw questioning the player at their camp is CampChallenge; an ambush standoff is AmbushStandoff; resisting a guard who has stopped one over a bounty is Arrest.
- ACTION: Crafting — Category: the speaker makes something for a person who asked: a smith forging a weapon or armor piece now or taking an order to collect later, cooking a meal, brewing a potion, or a smith handing over a finished order. Only when the speaker commits in this line to making a specific item for someone, or hands over a finished order being collected now; work already under way, offering services, and discussing or refusing a job are words. Drinks and other goods already made are sold (Economy) or given (Items). In the intent, name the item and who it is for.
- ACTION: Economy — Category: money changing hands now: buying or selling, paying, tipping, rewarding or refunding someone, collecting what is owed or offered, and opening, adding to, paying off, reducing or forgiving a tab or recurring payment. The speaker choosing to pay, tip or reward counts even unasked, as does billing the player, who is asked to confirm; a sale, a new tab or billing anyone else needs their agreement in this line. Quoted prices, haggling, money asked for or promised, and coin already handed over are words. Not here: unpriced hand-overs (Items), a smith's order (Crafting), retainers (Employment), bounties (Arrest), the Final Audit (Taxes).
- ACTION: Employment — Category: the speaker working for the player as a retainer or hold steward: hire the speaker to run a venture off-screen; appoint or relieve a hold steward; pay back-wages, grant a raise or settle on a compromise; grant, refuse or forgive a loan; hear out or brush off a work grievance; hand over earnings or the hold vault; or let a retainer go. Only when one of these is settled in this exchange; open offers and plans for later are words. Money between the player and their own worker is here, not Economy. Not the speaker's job for someone else, a traveling companion (Companionship), or a whole outlaw camp (OutlawCamp).
- ACTION: food_and_drink — Food, drink, hunger, and consumption actions. Select this when Solveig Chill-Wind wants to drink alcohol or ask the player for food.
- ACTION: health_and_recovery — Physical treatment and recovery actions. Select this when Solveig Chill-Wind needs embedded arrows or bolts removed, or is recovering from intoxication.
- ACTION: leashed_leashLeashed PARAMS: {"intent":"Who puts the collar on you, who holds it (or None), how, and why. Example — Bob puts a rope leash on my neck and holds it."} — Someone else (including the player) puts a new collar and leash on you. Use when narration already said you were leashed. Dialogue may object; still pick this so the game applies it. Not when you collar someone else, and not for changing or removing an existing leash.
- ACTION: Magic — Category: magic cast or taught right now, outside a fight: cast a spell the speaker knows (heal a wound, light the way, raise a ward, strike a beast), teach the player a spell or learn one from them, or, for a master of the Voice, teach a word of a Shout. Only when the cast or the lesson happens in this line; readying a spell 'in case', boasts and lessons promised for later are words. Attacking a person to start a fight is Combat.
- ACTION: Outfit — Category: the speaker's own clothes and gear, changed right now: put on or take off named pieces, strip down or dress again, save what they wear as a named outfit or change into one, and set or clear the outfit they change into by themselves in a situation (town, adventure, home, sleep, combat, rain, snow). Only when the speaker does it in this line; talk about clothes or changing later is words. Not giving, selling or trading items, or the player's own gear.
- ACTION: StartIntimateScenes PARAMS: {"intent":"What you intended to do when selected this action. Specify your intent and all potential participants including justification for your choice."} — Intimate actions - start sex, start platonic or romantic care action(hugging, kissing), join ongoing sex(there should be real sex scene not flirting or touching)
- ACTION: TagAlong — Category: the speaker walks along behind the player for a while without joining as a companion, agreeing in this line to come along now (to the inn, the ruin, the next town); or stops tagging along and goes back to their own business. Only for what happens in this line; 'maybe later' is not. Joining for the long road is Companionship, and so is telling someone already tagging along to wait at this spot or follow again. Going ahead to a place to wait for the player is Journeys.
- ACTION: None — The dialogue is purely conversational with no implied action.
